<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<beans xmlns="http://www.springframework.org/schema/beans"
       xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xmlns:context="http://www.springframework.org/schema/context"
       xmlns:mvc="http://www.springframework.org/schema/mvc"
       xsi:schemaLocation="
       http://www.springframework.org/schema/beans http://www.springframework.org/schema/beans/spring-beans.xsd
       http://www.springframework.org/schema/context http://www.springframework.org/schema/context/spring-context.xsd
       http://www.springframework.org/schema/mvc http://www.springframework.org/schema/mvc/spring-mvc.xsd">

    <!-- Enable component scanning -->
    <context:component-scan base-package="com.pos"/>

    <!-- Enable annotation-driven MVC -->
    <mvc:annotation-driven/>

    <!-- Enable CORS -->
    <mvc:cors>
        <mvc:mapping path="/customer/**"
                     allowed-origins="http://localhost:5173"
                     allowed-methods="GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS"
                     allowed-headers="*"
                     allow-credentials="true"
                     max-age="3600"/>
        <mvc:mapping path="/item/**"
                     allowed-origins="http://localhost:5173"
                     allowed-methods="GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS"
                     allowed-headers="*"
                     allow-credentials="true"
                     max-age="3600"/>
        <mvc:mapping path="/order/**"
                     allowed-origins="http://localhost:5173"
                     allowed-methods="GET, POST, OPTIONS"
                     allowed-headers="*"
                     allow-credentials="true"
                     max-age="3600"/>
    </mvc:cors>

</beans>

<!--

you don't need servlet-config.xml. It's legacy XML configuration that's been replaced by WebMvcConfig.java.

Why It's Not Used
Current Configuration:

web.xml loads WebMvcConfig.java (Java-based configuration)
WebMvcConfig.java handles everything this XML file does
What servlet-config.xml Does (Replaced by WebMvcConfig):

XML Feature	WebMvcConfig Equivalent
<context:component-scan>	@ComponentScan("com.pos")
<mvc:annotation-driven/>	@EnableWebMvc
<mvc:cors>	@CrossOrigin on controllers
CORS Configuration
In servlet-config.xml (unused):



xml
<mvc:cors>
    <mvc:mapping path="/customer/**" allowed-origins="http://localhost:5173" .../>
</mvc:cors>
In Controllers (active):



java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/customer")
@CrossOrigin(origins = "http://localhost:5173")  // This is used
public class CustomerController { }
Can You Delete It?
Yes. You can safely delete servlet-config.xml because:

It's never loaded by web.xml
All its functionality is in WebMvcConfig.java
CORS is handled by @CrossOrigin annotations on controllers
Delete it to clean up the unused legacy XML configuration.

-->

